 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 525966,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is a reasonable estimate for the length of a hallway: 2.5 kilometers, 2.5 meters, or 2.5 centimeters?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Think of a yardstick, which is roughly the length of a meter. A short hallway could be 2.5 meters long.</p>\n<p>A kilometer is not a reasonable length for a hallway. Even one kilometer would be one thousand meters long. A 2.5-kilometer hallway would be 2,500 meters long.</p>\n<p>The ruler you used in elementary school probably had 12 inches on one side and 30 centimeters on the other side. A 2.5-centimeter hallway would be shorter than your 12-inch ruler. This is not a reasonable length.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "2.5 m"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
